      "itemDescription": "Lockdowns kept Americans off the road in the first months of the pandemic. State Farm, the largest auto insurer in the U.S., returned $2 billion in premiums to car-insurance customers, and saw its 2020 profits fall 33.1%, to $3.7 billion. The 99-year-old Illinois-based company also swung to an underwriting loss of $1.6 billion in its homeowners insurance business \u201cdue to significant catastrophe activity across the country.\u201d",
